# Changelog

All notable changes to `@re-cinq/hal-engine` are documented here.

The format is [Keep a Changelog 1.1.0](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), and this project adheres to
[Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html). Entries are written for somebody installing the
package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.

## [Unreleased]

### Added

- Tool input is now validated against each tool's declared `inputSchema` before its executor runs.
  A call the schema rejects — a missing required property, a value of the wrong type or outside its
  `enum` — is returned to the model as a normal tool result describing the failure, instead of
  reaching your executor. Migration: an executor that hand-validated its input now receives only
  input the schema already accepts, and a tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its
  own error message stops seeing it. Validation enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` only;
  extra properties pass through unchanged, values are never coerced or defaulted, and rejection
  messages name property paths and constraints but never property values.

